  "project_description": "Elasticsearch Helper Content module provides tools to create Elasticsearch indices for content entities in Drupal UI.\n\n Back to top \n\n Requirements \n \n Drupal 9 or 10 \n Elasticsearch Helper module \n Elasticsearch Helper Index Management module \n \n Back to top \n\n Installation \n Elasticsearch Helper Views module can be installed via the\n\n standard Drupal installation process .\n\n \n Install Elasticsearch search engine ( how-to ). \n Install and enable Elasticsearch Helper module. \n Install and enable Elasticsearch Helper Index Management module. \n Install and enable Elasticsearch Helper Content module. \n \n Back to top \n\n Usage \n \n Go to /admin/config/search/elasticsearch_helper/index \n Click on the Add content index button. \n Fill the form with label, index name information, select the entity fields you want to have indexed, and save the form. \n Click on the Setup button next to the index plugin to create the index in Elasticsearch. \n Back to top",
